NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
GAMEHUB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://gamehub.mhhorizons.com
ADMIN_EMAILS=shivam63pandey@gmail.com
PREMIUM_SESSION_TICKET_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-production-secret
GAMEHUB_PREMIUM_FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS=premium/firebase_credentials/config.js
GAMEHUB_PREMIUM_FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=premium/firebase_credentials/serviceAccount.json
MULTIPLAYER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://gamehub.mhhorizons.com
ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL_AUTH=false
# Notes:
# - Keep real .env files private. This file is placeholders only.
# - GAMEHUB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS accepts a comma-separated list when multiple domains are needed.
# - ADMIN_EMAILS accepts a comma-separated list. Production should set this explicitly.
# - If ADMIN_EMAILS is missing outside production, GameHub uses a local/dev fallback for the first admin only.
# - GAMEHUB_PREMIUM_FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS must point to a readable file, not a directory.
# - The credential file must contain the existing browser firebaseConfig object:
#   const firebaseConfig = { apiKey: "...", authDomain: "...", projectId: "...", appId: "..." };
# - It may be an absolute path outside the repo on a VPS.
# - GAMEHUB_PREMIUM_FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT is server-only and is used by Space Race multiplayer token verification.
# - The feedback system also uses the server-only Firebase Admin service account for Firestore storage.
# - Internal analytics also uses the server-only Firebase Admin service account for Firestore storage.
# - Admin user/payment visibility also uses the server-only Firebase Admin service account for read-only Auth/Firestore access.
# - Without Firebase Admin credentials, feedback/analytics and Phase 5 admin audit/manual entitlement
#   support fall back to .gamehub-data/ only in local/dev.
# - Do not commit or serve config.js/serviceAccount.json/raw credential folders.
